TITLE:: FxLoop
summary:: a delay line with feedback that needs no LocalIn
categories:: Libraries>FxKit
related:: Classes/FxParamUnit, Classes/LocalBuf

DESCRIPTION::
A SynthDef can have one LocalIn, and two effects of this family must be able to share a graph, so feedback goes through a buffer: one LocalBuf per channel, written at a phasor, read as far behind as you like, as often as you like. Use it inside a SynthDef function. Read first, then write what the reads made. The shortest delay is a block and a few samples. It costs 4 bytes a frame of the server's real time memory.

code::
{
	var sig = Decay2.kr(Impulse.kr(1), 0.01, 0.1) * PinkNoise.ar(0.2 ! 2);
	var l = FxLoop(2, 1);
	var y = l.read(0.25);
	l.write(sig + (y * 0.6));
	sig + y
}.play;
::

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: new
run: 1 goes on writing, 0 stands still.
